              "login": "ghosttT0"
            },
            "body": "Independent verification that this bug is real (I opened a duplicate PR #62323 against current main before finding this one — closed mine, the evidence belongs here):\n\nReproduced the unbounded loop against `_generate_with_builtin_tools`: with `request.max_tool_calls = 2` and a model that emits a builtin tool call on every turn, the loop performed 50+ engine round-trips (stopped only by an external emergency cap), while the request carried and echoed `max_tool_calls=2` as if a quota were in effect. The field has zero consumers in serving code (declared, echoed, and copied only), and every turn re-derives `sampling_params.max_tokens` from the full remaining budget, so nothing else bounds the loop.\n\nThis PR's approach matches what I'd independently implement. Hope the verification helps get it reviewed — happy to test the branch against current main if useful.",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-18T16:20:55Z",
